rs/iap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/managers/iap#restore-and-events","content":"Restore and events"},"668":{"id":"/en/usage/managers/iap-6","page_id":"/en/usage/managers/iap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/usage/managers/iap#api","content":"API"},"669":{"id":"/en/usage/managers/iap-7","page_id":"/en/usage/managers/iap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/managers/iap","content":"`IAPManager` uses Unity IAP 5.4.1 `StoreController` APIs for store connection, product lookup, purchase, pending-order retry, and restoration. In player builds, it confirms an order only after its reward has been persisted."},"670":{"id":"/en/usage/managers/iap-8","page_id":"/en/usage/managers/iap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/managers/iap","content":"`com.unity.purchasing` 5.4.1 is an AchEngine dependency, and `AchManagerInstaller` registers `IAPManager` automatically."},"671":{"id":"/en/usage/managers/iap-9","page_id":"/en/usage/managers/iap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/managers/iap#quick-setup","content":"Product IDs must exactly match Google Play Console or App Store Connect. For player builds, configure products and a receipt validator before initialization."},"672":{"id":"/en/usage/managers/iap-10","page_id":"/en/usage/managers/iap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/managers/iap#editor-fake-store-testing","content":"In the Unity Editor, `IAPManager` explicitly selects Unity IAP's `fake` store.\nOnly in the Editor, a Fake Store order is automatically confirmed when both\n`ReceiptValidator` and `PurchaseProcessor` are unset. This lets you test purchase\nbuttons, completion events, and popup flow without making a real payment or\ncalling a backend."},"673":{"id":"/en/usage/managers/iap-11","page_id":"/en/usage/managers/iap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/managers/iap#editor-fake-store-testing","content":"This behavior is compiled only under `UNITY_EDITOR`. Android, iOS, and other\nplayer builds still require a receipt validator or fulfillment processor before\na purchase can start. The editor fake order is not granted as a real purchase."},"674":{"id":"/en/usage/managers/iap-12","page_id":"/en/usage/managers/iap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/managers/iap#editor-fake-store-testing","content":"The Full Sample `PurchasePopup` also enables its purchase buttons without a\nvalidator in the Editor. Assign the game-specific server validator to the\n`Receipt Validator` field for real builds."},"675":{"id":"/en/usage/managers/iap-13","page_id":"/en/usage/managers/iap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/managers/iap#editor-fake-store-testing","content":"Implement `IIAPReceiptValidator` in the game project. Authenticate the player, send platform transaction data to the backend, and persist rewards idempotently on the server."},"676":{"id":"/en/usage/managers/iap-14","page_id":"/en/usage/managers/iap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/managers/iap#purchase-requests","content":"`PurchaseAsync` returns only after store purchase, server fulfillment, and order confirmation are complete. In player builds, without a validator or processor, it does not open the purchase dialog. The Editor uses the Fake Store flow described above."},"677":{"id":"/en/usage/managers/iap-15","page_id":"/en/usage/managers/iap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/managers/iap#purchase-requests","content":"Status"},"678":{"id":"/en/usage/managers/iap-16","page_id":"/en/usage/managers/iap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/managers/iap#purchase-requests","content":"Meaning"},"679":{"id":"/en/usage/managers/iap-17","page_id":"/en/usage/managers/iap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/managers/iap#purchase-requests","content":"`Confirmed`"},"680":{"id":"/en/usage/managers/iap-18","page_id":"/en/usage/managers/iap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/usage/managers/iap#purchase-requests","content":"Receipt validated, reward persisted, and store order confirmed"},"681":{"id":"/en/usage/m